even dozens of hours in the Legend of  Zelda breath of the wild remains packed  with mechanics and concepts that were  still finding out about with so many  veiled secrets still hidden in its  mysterious world we've compiled nine  more useful things to know to help you  on your journey  be wary there are potential spoilers  ahead if you love this video like it and  subscribe to our YouTube channel for  more features on breath of the wild and  be sure to watch our previous video on  the nine things I wish I knew before  starting  [Music]  early on if you need to swim across a  body of water but don't have the  necessary stamina and speed to clear the  distance you can take off your clothes  to swim faster though make sure to put  your armor back on when there are  enemies in the water as your defense is  incredibly low while naked utilize this  technique until you acquire the Zora  armor which greatly enhances your  swimming speed while providing you  defensive power  when you're traveling in between towns  you'll encounter travelling merchants  who can sell you various equipment or  cooking ingredients be sure to browse  their wares when possible for supplies  you might need however when it rains  merchants bust out their rare items for  example a merchant that typically sells  the raw meat ingredient during sunny  weather will list the better more  effective raw prime meat ingredient when  it rains if storm clouds start to appear  seek out merchants in the area you never  know what rare items you might be able  to purchase lighting grass on fire  creates a temporary updraft that you can  use to skyrocket yourself up into the  air with your glider this has a variety  of applications such as creating height  between you and an approaching guardian  or propelling yourself upward to give  you more time in the air  [Music]  it's actually possible to ride wild  animals such as bears and deer like you  would a horse so long as you approach it  carefully and with stealth bonuses  activated unfortunately wild animals  aren't the most useful or reliable  mounts as they're far less compliant  than horses  you also can't register them at stables  for future travels despite these  limitations riding wild animals is a fun  novelty what we're taking advantage of  when the opportunity presents itself  after all who doesn't want to ride a  bear  [Music]  while climbing if you jump when your  stamina wheel is in the red you'll  propel yourself upward twice the usual  distance this is a handy last resort  technique that can be a lifesaver when  you're just about to reach the top of a  mountain but can't make it by climbing  alone  [Music]  if you miss an enemy with an arrow don't  worry it's possible to pick it back up  the same works for enemy arrows which  you can pick up when they land at your  feet you can even retrieve the arrows  that gets stuck to your shield by  putting it away this is a great way to  farm hundreds of arrows by the way  regardless when a battle is over  make sure to mine the battlefield for  all the arrows that missed their mark  similar to The Legend of Zelda Wind  Waker HD you can take selfies in the  breath of the wild with your sheikah  slates camera simply turn on the camera  with the L button and then press X to  activate self portrait mode moving the  left stick in different directions  changes links pose while in this mode  maximizing the photos social media  effectiveness  it's made apparent early on that you can  scan amiibo to get new weapons and items  but if you scanned amiibo of classic  Zelda characters you can get special  armor and weapons from past games for  example when you scan the toon link  amiibo you have the chance of acquiring  winwaker inspired armor pieces you can  even obtain new mounts like the iconic  Epona  which you can get when you scan the  Super Smash Brothers series link amiibo  it's worth noting that each amiibo can  only be scanned once per day and that  items are randomized in addition certain  items are only available to its  respective amiibo so don't expect to get  sheikhs mask from the Ganondorf amiibo  if you're interested in dawning on the  classic link outfits from past games be  sure to take advantage of breadth of the  wilds of meebo functionality do whatever  it takes to make it happen  whether that be scanning in your fans  expansive collection of Zelda amiibo or  forking over your life savings to buy  your own  [Music]  have you ever recklessly let your trusty  steed die in the middle of a battle and  spent the rest of your journey in a  debilitating state of regret and  self-loathing opponent jr. I'm sorry I'm  so sorry  fret not it's actually possible to bring  your horse back to life but you can't do  it with the help of the folks at the  stable rather you need to seek out the  help of melania the great horse fairy to  find ur head to the licked our region to  the south and find the Highland stable  from there head south east towards the  horse god bridge when you reach the end  of the path you'll find what looks like  a great fairy fountain examine it in pay  Melania the flat fee of a thousand  rupees to access her services talk to  her again and she'll work her magic to  bring your steed back from the grave  note that you can do this as many times  as you'd like at no additional rupy cost  to you so you never have to go back to  that dark place of grief ever again  what secrets have you found let us know  in the comments below and for more  coverage on The Legend of Zelda breath  of the wild including our full review be  sure to subscribe to our YouTube channel  [Music]
 

